---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="How SmallNestDecor earns money from affiliate links, including the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold">Affiliate Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-cocoa">Last updated: October 20, 2026</p>
    <div class="prose-nest mt-6">
      <p>SmallNestDecor is reader-supported, and we want to be completely plain about how that works.</p>
      <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
      <p>{siteConfig.name} is a participant in the <strong>Amazon Services LLC Associates Program</strong>, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com. When you click an Amazon link on this site and make a purchase, we may earn a small commission. The price you pay is exactly the same.</p>
      <h2>Other affiliate programs</h2>
      <p>From time to time we may also link to other retailers (for example home and storage stores) through affiliate programs. Posts that contain affiliate links are labelled with a short disclosure directly under the introduction, so you always know before you click.</p>
      <h2>Our promise</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We only link to products that fit the guide and that we would genuinely suggest to a friend with the same small space.</li>
        <li>A commission never buys a recommendation, a ranking, or a kind word.</li>
        <li>If a product disappoints us, we say so or remove it.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>This site may also display advertising served by networks such as Google AdSense and, in future, Mediavine or Raptive. Advertisers do not influence our editorial content.</p>
      <p>Questions about any of this? Write to <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
